{"v":2,"s":"p","w":7,"steps":[{"t":"read","h":"Mass and weight","b":"<p><b>Mass</b> (masa, kg) is the amount of matter and is the same everywhere. <b>Weight</b> (težina, N) is the force with which a body presses on its support or pulls on a hanger:</p><div class=\"fx\">G = m · g</div><p>On the Moon (g ≈ 1.6 m/s²) your mass is the same, but your weight is about 6 times smaller.</p>"},{"t":"read","h":"Friction","b":"<p><b>Friction</b> (trenje) opposes sliding:</p><div class=\"fx\">F<sub>tr</sub> = μ · N</div><p>N is the normal force (on a horizontal surface N = mg), μ the coefficient of friction. Friction depends on the surfaces, not on the contact area.</p><div class=\"callout\">Rubber soles on asphalt versus on ice — the same shoe, a very different μ.</div><figure class=\"fig\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Left: friction always points against the motion. Right: a spring stretches in proportion to the force — Hooke’s law.\"><defs><marker id=\"ah\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"ink\"/></marker><marker id=\"ahc\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" class=\"a\"/></marker></defs><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"90\" class=\"k\" /><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"8\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"24\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"18\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"34\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"28\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"44\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"38\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"54\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"48\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"64\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"68\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"84\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"94\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"88\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"98\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"114\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"124\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"118\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"134\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"128\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"144\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"138\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"154\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"148\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><line x1=\"164\" y1=\"90\" x2=\"158\" y2=\"98\" class=\"km\" /><rect x=\"60\" y=\"52\" width=\"60\" height=\"38\" rx=\"3\" class=\"sf\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"71\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"71\" class=\"kc\" marker-end=\"url(#ahc)\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"62\" class=\"acc\" font-weight=\"700\">F</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"86\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"86\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"10\">F_tr</text><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"30\" class=\"k\" /><path d=\"M200 30 L228 38 L212 46 L228 54 L212 62 L228 70 L212 78 L228 86 L212 94 L220 106\" class=\"kc\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"106\" width=\"24\" height=\"20\" rx=\"2\" class=\"a\"/><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"92\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"106\" class=\"km\" /><text x=\"270\" y=\"103\" font-size=\"11\">Δl</text><line x1=\"220\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"220\" y2=\"150\" class=\"k\" marker-end=\"url(#ah)\"/><text x=\"236\" y=\"148\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\">F = kΔl</text></svg><figcaption>Left: friction always points against the motion. Right: a spring stretches in proportion to the force — Hooke’s law.</figcaption></figure>"},{"t":"read","h":"Elastic force","b":"<p>A stretched spring pulls back with a force proportional to the stretch — <b>Hooke’s law</b>:</p><div class=\"fx\">F = k · Δl</div><p>k is the spring constant in N/m. At constant velocity the net force is zero, so the push equals the friction.</p>"},{"t":"ex","q":"A 10 kg crate is pushed at constant speed, μ = 0.4 (g = 10). Push force?","s":["Constant speed → net force 0 → push = friction.","N = mg = 100 N.","F_tr = 0.4 · 100 = 40 N."],"a":"40 N"},{"t":"num","q":"Weight of 50 kg (g = 10)?","a":500,"u":"N","e":"mg."},{"t":"num","q":"Friction on 30 kg with μ = 0.2 (g = 10)?","a":60,"u":"N","e":"0.2 · 300."},{"t":"num","q":"Spring with k = 100 N/m stretched 0.15 m. Force?","a":15,"u":"N","e":"kΔl."},{"t":"mc","q":"A body moving at constant velocity has a net force of:","o":["zero","equal to its weight","equal to friction","impossible to say"],"a":0,"e":"Newton’s first law."},{"t":"num","q":"Stretch of a spring with k = 200 N/m under 10 N?","a":0.05,"u":"m","e":"10/200.","tol":0.001}]}